    {
      "id": 135328,
      "name": "metlarcturus",
      "username": "metlarcturus",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/metlarcturus/{size}/2210_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-03-04T15:49:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This scenario looks like a lot of fun, but I had a few questions about spawning:</p><p>a) How many humans do you spawn at the beginning of the game?</p><p>b) How many humans do you spawn at the end of each round?</p><p>c) Do you spawn all four raptors to start the game?</p><p>d) Can dinosaurs respawn after being killed? If they can, how does that work (i.e. do all dead dinosaurs spawn at the beginning of their turn)?</p><p>And finally, though not spawn related,</p><p>e) \"Thugs will move towards the closest non-Thug target with the lowest Health that they can see.\" Are they prioritizing low health or distance? That is, if a thug can see a 4 health target 2 hexes away and a 1 health target 6 hexes away, which one will he move toward?</p><p>I'm looking forward to trying this out!</p>",
      "post_number": 11,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:11:22.879Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 12535,
      "topic_slug": "i-made-a-fully-coop-tactics-scenario-where-dinosaurs-invade-megalopolis",
