    {
      "id": 135330,
      "name": "SALLstice",
      "username": "SALLstice",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/848f3c/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-03-05T20:06:40.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I've updated the scenario a little bit. &nbsp;<span>I fixed some formatting and how the rules sectioned out for hopefully more clarity.</span></p><p>Mostly, though, I pretty completely redid how the villians move and act. &nbsp;They each have a different 'flavor' now.</p><p><strong>The T-Rex goes after the biggest target he can see.<br>The Raptors now use pack hunting and go after whomever hurt them last.<br>Thugs pick off the weakest targets around, usually Civilians.</strong></p><p>The idea was to give the villain targets some differentiation and more character.</p><p>If you have a chance to give this scenario a try, please let me know how it goes for you!! :D</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2><a href=\"http://nerdaphernalia.blogspot.com/2015/03/dino-riot-v-10.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Dino Riot (v 1.1)</a></h2>",
      "post_number": 13,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:11:23.022Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 2,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 10.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 12535,
      "topic_slug": "i-made-a-fully-coop-tactics-scenario-where-dinosaurs-invade-megalopolis",
      "display_username": "SALLstice",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "link_counts": [
        {
          "url": "http://nerdaphernalia.blogspot.com/2015/03/dino-riot-v-10.html",
          "internal": false,
          "reflection": false,
          "title": "Nerdaphernalia: Dino Riot! (v 1.1)",
          "clicks": 2
        }
      ],
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I&#39;ve updated the scenario a little bit. &nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">I fixed some formatting and how the rules sectioned out for hopefully more clarity.</span></p><p>Mostly, though, I pretty completely redid how the villians move and act. &nbsp;They each have a different &#39;flavor&#39; now.</p><p><strong>The T-Rex goes after the biggest target he can see.<br />The Raptors now use pack hunting and go after whomever hurt them last.<br />Thugs pick off the weakest targets around, usually Civilians.</strong></p><p>The idea was to give the villain targets some differentiation and more character.</p><p>If you have a chance to give this scenario a try, please let me know how it goes for you!! :D</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h2><a href=\"http://nerdaphernalia.blogspot.com/2015/03/dino-riot-v-10.html\">Dino Riot (v 1.1)</a></h2>",
