      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"metlarcturus\"]\n\na) How many humans do you spawn at the beginning of the game?\n\n \n[/quote]\n \n\n All of them \n\n \n[quote=\"metlarcturus\"]\n \n\nb) How many humans do you spawn at the end of each round?\n\n \n[/quote]\n \n\n All of them \n\n \n[quote=\"metlarcturus\"]\n \n\nc) Do you spawn all four raptors to start the game?\n\n \n[/quote]\n \n\n All of them \n\n \n[quote=\"metlarcturus\"]\n \n\nd) Can dinosaurs respawn after being killed? If they can, how does that work (i.e. do all dead dinosaurs spawn at the beginning of their turn)?\n\n \n[/quote]\n \n\n All o.... er, I mean, yeah, Dinosaurs spawn at the start of their turn then they move on that same turn. &nbsp;It&#39;s stated in there, but certainly could be made more clear. &nbsp;I have a habit of writing rules so they make sense to me, and polishing them up after a week or so of feedback. &nbsp;So expect that soon. \n\n \n[quote=\"metlarcturus\"]\n \n\ne) &quot;Thugs will move towards the closest non-Thug target with the lowest Health that they can see.&quot; Are they prioritizing low health or distance? That is, if a thug can see a 4 health target 2 hexes away and a 1 health target 6 hexes away, which one will he move toward?I&#39;m looking forward to trying this out!\n\n[/quote]\n\n&lt;strike&gt;First distance, then Health. &nbsp;Also will make this more clear.&lt;/strike&gt;<br />EDIT: This is not true anymore :O\n\n&nbsp;\n\n Thanks for the questions! More feedback is always good. \n\n EDIT: I&#39;m also working on a way to scale with number of Heroes, so you probably won&#39;t always spawn all the raptors and humans every time, but for now it seems to work well enough. \n",
